diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..113211e 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,8 +2,42 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Delivery behavior
+
+When an event is created on a board, each active webhook subscribed to its action gets
+one asynchronous HTTP POST. The JSON body contains the event's `id`, `action`,
+`created_at`, `eventable` (card or comment), `board`, and `creator`.
+
+Requests include:
+
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Delivery-Id`: the unique delivery ID, stable across duplicate job execution
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the event's UTC creation time (ISO 8601)
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, using
+  the webhook's signing secret
+
+A `2xx` response is a success. Other HTTP statuses (including redirects) and network
+errors are failures. Requests time out after ten seconds; redirects are not followed.
+Only public HTTP(S) destinations are allowed.
+
+Each webhook/event pair has one delivery record, and duplicate jobs cannot send it
+again. **There are no automatic retries**, even after a timeout: the receiver may
+already have accepted the POST. This provides at-most-once sending, not a guarantee
+of exactly-once processing at the receiver. Receivers should use the event `id` as an
+idempotency key when applying side effects. Delivery logs expire, so they are not a
+permanent deduplication ledger or a replay API.
+
+A webhook is automatically deactivated after at least **ten consecutive failures
+spanning at least one hour**. A successful delivery resets the streak. Reactivating
+also resets it, and queued deliveries are not sent while a webhook is inactive.
+
+Delivery logs contain the state, request headers, HTTP status or transport error,
+and event details. Logs are retained for **seven days** and cleaned every 15 minutes.
+The signature is omitted from the delivery-history API.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
+
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
 
 __Response:__
